From: 77450danik <ddziuba1@stu.vistula.edu.pl>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: Title bars in the mode of Windows, over a backdrop; the dark mode for programs.

The title bars and frames follow the mode of Windows (desk.cpl,
Personalization; SystemUsesLightTheme), not the visual style's colours,
which follow the programs' mode: white with black text in the light mode,
#202020 with white text in the dark one, the Windows 11 caption buttons
dark or light with them. A program can ask otherwise for its window, as in
Windows 11 (DWMWA_USE_IMMERSIVE_DARK_MODE, DWMWA_CAPTION_COLOR,
DWMWA_TEXT_COLOR, DWMWA_BORDER_COLOR, through dwmapi).

With an effect chosen for them (HKCU\Software\Arctic\Caption), a
top-level window's title bar is drawn on the colour dwm.exe keys, and
DWMWA_ARCTIC_CAPTION tells dwm.exe what goes behind it: acrylic, a blur or
a see-through tint, its colour, opacity and blur. WM_SETTINGCHANGE
"ImmersiveColorSet" reads it all anew and redraws the frames.

What programs ask of the dark mode by ordinal, as Notepad++ and Qt do:
ShouldSystemUseDarkMode, ShouldAppsUseDarkMode, SetPreferredAppMode,
AllowDarkModeForWindow and the rest, from the same settings.

A property page drew its background, the visual style's tab texture, with
the theme opened for it before the style changed: it stayed light in the
dark scheme. That theme is opened anew on WM_THEMECHANGED.
